---
// Short answers, each checked against the README, the terms and the privacy policy.
import { support } from '../../data/patchr/links';
import ExternalLink from '../ExternalLink.astro';
import Icon from '../Icon.astro';
---

<section class="faq section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="container faq__inner">
    <h2 class="p-h2" id="faq-title" data-reveal="lines">Questions.</h2>
    <div class="faq__list" data-reveal="fade">
      <details>
        <summary>Is Patchr free?<Icon name="plus" class="faq__icon" /></summary>
        <div class="faq__answer"><p>Yes. It costs nothing and there’s nothing to buy.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Who can use its commands?<Icon name="plus" class="faq__icon" /></summary>
        <div class="faq__answer">
          <p>
            Members with Manage Server, by default. Change it in Server Settings, under Integrations, then Patchr.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does it read my server’s messages?<Icon name="plus" class="faq__icon" /></summary>
        <div class="faq__answer">
          <p>
            No. Patchr doesn’t read messages, member lists or direct messages, and it doesn’t ask Discord for the
            permissions that would let it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What does it keep, and for how long?<Icon name="plus" class="faq__icon" /></summary>
        <div class="faq__answer">
          <p>
            Only what it needs to post: your settings, your feeds and a record of each post. Remove Patchr and
            everything it stored for your server is deleted. The <a href="/patchr/privacy/">privacy policy</a> has
            the details.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I run my own copy?<Icon name="plus" class="faq__icon" /></summary>
        <div class="faq__answer"><p>Yes. It’s MIT licensed and ships with a Docker setup. See above.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Where do I get help?<Icon name="plus" class="faq__icon" /></summary>
        <div class="faq__answer">
          <p>
            In the <ExternalLink href={support}>support server</ExternalLink>. Bug reports and ideas are welcome there
            too.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
